<div class="two-col-layout">

<h2>8. Implementation and DevOps</h2>
<p>Source code is organised by business domain rather than technical layer. The protech_project package holds settings with environment-driven secrets, URL routing, a Jinja2 environment shim exposing url_for and csrf_field helpers for legacy template compatibility, cache utilities, and a JSON /health/ endpoint for monitoring.</p>
<p>Caching in protech_project/cache_utils.py stores worker search results for three hundred seconds and service categories for six hundred seconds. invalidate_workers_cache() runs when new reviews alter rating aggregates. Continuous integration sets USE_LOCMEM_CACHE so tests execute without a live Redis daemon.</p>
<p>Structured logging writes to stdout and logs/django.log with per-application loggers (users, bookings, escrow). The Docker entrypoint runs migrations, collectstatic, seed_demo when the database is empty, and starts Gunicorn—enabling evaluators to run docker compose up --build and access http://localhost immediately.</p>


    <div class="figure-box">
      <table><tr><th>Rubric requirement</th><th>Implementation</th><th>Evidence</th></tr><tr><td>Django + templates</td><td>Django 5.2 + Jinja2</td><td>templates/, jinja2_env.py</td></tr><tr><td>Auth &amp; RBAC</td><td>Login, @user_type_required</td><td>users/decorators.py</td></tr><tr><td>Password reset</td><td>Django token flow</td><td>/password-reset/</td></tr><tr><td>Admin / CMS</td><td>Django Admin</td><td>/admin/</td></tr><tr><td>Docker + Redis</td><td>Four-service Compose</td><td>docker-compose.yml</td></tr><tr><td>Tests + CI</td><td>17 passing tests</td><td>.github/workflows/ci.yml</td></tr><tr><td>Logging</td><td>Per-app loggers</td><td>settings.py LOGGING</td></tr></table>
    </div>
<div class="figure-caption">Table 5: Academic rubric alignment (summary)</div>

<h2>9. Testing and Evaluation</h2>
<p>Quality assurance follows a pragmatic test pyramid. Unit tests validate model constraints and relationships. Integration tests in users/tests_integration.py exercise the health endpoint, email login, role-based access denial, and password reset availability. Escrow integration tests confirm wallet debits and payment status transitions.</p>
<p>GitHub Actions workflow ci.yml runs on push to main: flake8 critical checks, migrations against ephemeral PostgreSQL, the full Django test suite, and a /health/ probe. At the time of writing, seventeen automated tests pass with USE_LOCMEM_CACHE enabled.</p>


    <div class="figure-box">
      <table><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Result</th><th>Benchmark</th></tr><tr><td>Automated tests</td><td>17 passing</td><td>Module requirement met</td></tr><tr><td>CI pipeline</td><td>Lint, migrate, test, health</td><td>GitHub Actions green</td></tr><tr><td>Deployment</td><td>docker compose up --build</td><td>Single-command demo</td></tr><tr><td>User roles</td><td>Client, worker, admin</td><td>RBAC verified</td></tr><tr><td>Escrow commission</td><td>5% default (configurable)</td><td>Live in services.py</td></tr><tr><td>Cache backend</td><td>Redis (prod) / locmem (CI)</td><td>Environment-aware</td></tr></table>
    </div>
<div class="figure-caption">Table 6: Evaluation metrics and outcomes</div>

<h2>10. Limitations</h2>
<p>Academic honesty requires explicit acknowledgment of constraints. ProTech uses demonstration wallet deposits rather than a licensed payment provider; worker subscription tiers are specified but not billed; messaging requires page refresh rather than WebSockets; test coverage excludes browser end-to-end automation; growth charts are illustrative rather than empirically validated; and legacy Flask/PHP artefacts remain in the repository for reference while Django is canonical.</p>

<h2>11. Conclusion and Future Work</h2>
<p>This paper has presented ProTech as a evolved, production-oriented marketplace replacing an earlier PHP prototype with a Django, PostgreSQL, Redis, and Docker stack. The platform integrates discovery, booking, messaging, reviews, escrow payments, caching, logging, automated testing, and continuous integration into a cohesive system suitable for master&#x27;s-level assessment and live defence demonstration.</p>
<p>Future work prioritises Stripe (or equivalent) integration for regulated payments, WorkerSubscription model implementation with search-ranking enforcement, WebSocket or Celery notifications, Selenium/Cypress end-to-end tests, geolocation-aware matching, and two-factor authentication. The modular domain architecture supports these increments without fundamental restructuring.</p>
<p>ProTech demonstrates that academic projects can meet rigorous full-stack criteria while addressing genuine marketplace problems—with transparent limitations and a credible path toward commercial deployment.</p>

